# Stations for ~/.local/bin/focus-music. One per line: a name, a tab, a URL.
#
# Tracked here rather than inside the helper, so adding a station is editing
# data rather than editing a script - and so a rebuilt machine has the same
# list. Comments and blank lines are ignored.
#
# WHY SOMAFM AND NOT A YOUTUBE LOFI CHANNEL
#
# These are direct audio URLs. They need no yt-dlp, no API, no key, and no
# resolving step that can break independently of the player - all six were
# checked returning audio/mpeg before being written down. A YouTube live stream
# needs yt-dlp to resolve it on every start, and the video id changes whenever
# the channel restarts, which turns a station into a thing that stops working
# for reasons nobody can see.
#
# yt-dlp is still declared, so pasting a YouTube or SoundCloud link at the
# helper works. It is just not what the defaults depend on.
#
# SomaFM is listener-supported and asks for a donation rather than serving ads:
# https://somafm.com/support/

